            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "What are we getting from doing this? In my mind language level 2 is mostly about supporting old Python 2 syntax (so that people don't have to update their files). But this just looks like it selects a method of optimization and doesn't actually change any behaviour. Possibly I'm missing something here though?\n\nWith that said, a bugfix PR may not be the place to change it.\n",
